expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{prop:causality-closure}
Every admissible residual-causality feature of a description
\(D \in \ensuremath{\mathsf{FATCD}}\) whose content takes one of the recognized forms below
classifies, within the covered scope, as one of
\begin{itemize}[topsep=2pt,itemsep=1pt]
  \item a \ensuremath{\mathrm{P4}} projection, as the primary classification when the
    feature is a directed transition, refinement, or staged-dependence
    record;
  \item a \ensuremath{\mathrm{P3}} projection, only when the feature is specifically a
    route/coherence comparison between generated same-source,
    same-target routes;
  \item a \ensuremath{\mathrm{P6}} projection, when the feature is a provenance or
    dependency audit;
  \item a composite of \ensuremath{\mathrm{P4}} and \ensuremath{\mathrm{P6}}, when directed dependence
    and provenance audit occur together in the same admissible feature;
  \item an outside-domain structure, when the feature requires
    metaphysical causation not amenable to honest bookkeeping.
\end{itemize}
Classification as \ensuremath{\mathrm{P5}} is inadmissible in the absence of quotient
packaging. Residual-causality content of these recognized forms therefore requires no
seventh role; content of none of these forms is governed by the recognition
hypothesis (Definition~\ref{def:recognition-hypothesis}).\footnote{The Lean declaration is a trivial single-record harness check: \texttt{classifyResidual} maps \texttt{RawKind.causality} to \texttt{composite}, whose \texttt{CoveredResidualClass} branch is \texttt{True}; the \ensuremath{\mathrm{P5}}-inadmissibility content of the proposition is absent and no universal residual-causality closure is established. See Appendix~\ref{app:mechanization} (\texttt{SixBirds.causality\_closure}).}

