expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{thm:sau-primitive-head-classification}
Let \(\mathfrak B\) be a reduced basic SAU boundary trace whose boundary expression has a primitive head constructor in \(\mathcal G_{\operatorname{Basic}}\).  Then \(\mathfrak B\) has a unique primitive profile label in \(\mathcal R_{\operatorname{Basic}}\), namely
\[
\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\rho_{\operatorname{Basic}}(\operatorname{Head}(C)).
\]
More explicitly:
\begin{enumerate}
\item if \(\operatorname{Head}(C)\) is a composite or power constructor, then \(\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\mathsf{RootComp}\);
\item if \(\operatorname{Head}(C)\) is a coefficient or standard-part constructor, then \(\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\mathsf{Coeff}\);
\item if \(\operatorname{Head}(C)\) is a projection or shadow constructor, then \(\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\mathsf{ProjShad}\);
\item if \(\operatorname{Head}(C)\) is a fixed-point or invariant constructor, then \(\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\mathsf{InvDesc}\);
\item if \(\operatorname{Head}(C)\) is a trace, norm, or symmetric aggregation constructor, then \(\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\mathsf{AggInv}\), with an induced invariant-descent audit when the aggregation is fixed by the declared symmetry;
\item if \(\operatorname{Head}(C)\) is a quotient or obstruction-class constructor, then \(\operatorname{Profile}(\mathfrak B)=\mathsf{ObsLed}\).
\end{enumerate}

